  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Row of Counters",
    "overview": "The system is a light, calm fintech desk on a near-white cool ground, with one thing that sets it apart: every payment rail is a counter (balcão) with its own painted sign. M-Pesa, e-Mola, Banco and Numerário each carry a fixed colour, and that colour follows the money everywhere it appears: the sign on a feed row, the segment in a stacked bar, the booth tile with today's float. Totals are never one blended number in one green. They are built from these channel colours, so every amount can be traced back to its rail.\n\nDensity is operational, not editorial. White cards (16px radius, a hairline border, a near-invisible shadow) sit on the ground with 10–20px gutters. Numbers are big, semibold and tabular. Copy is plain Portuguese in sentence case. Green does the system's own work: actions, selection, and settled or healthy state. Status gets its own distinct hues (burnt orange, magenta-crimson, teal), so no status colour ever reads as a channel. Motion is reserved for state changes: a payment arriving, a count bumping, a panel entering. Each one lasts about 180–240ms, eases out, and resolves to its final state under reduced motion.\n\nThe data is sample data and the interface says so. A dashed \"Dados fictícios\" tag with an e-Mola-yellow dot sits permanently in the top bar.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One cool-neutral ground (`ground`) under white cards; flat tonal layering with only hairline borders and a whisper shadow.",
      "Four channel identities as solid, squared painted-sign tags in bold short caps.",
      "Green means action, selection, or settled state. Red belongs to M-Pesa alone.",
      "Geist throughout with tabular numerals. Geist Mono only for transaction IDs and payment references.",
      "Pill-shaped controls (buttons, nav items, search, selects) against squarer containers (tiles 12px, cards 16px, tags 4px)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Red Rule",
        "body": "Red (`mpesa`) means M-Pesa and nothing else. Danger is magenta-crimson (`danger`), never red.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sign Belongs to the Rail Rule",
        "body": "A channel colour appears only where that channel's money is shown: its tag, its chart segment, its booth. Never use a channel hue for status, decoration or emphasis.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Green Is the System Rule",
        "body": "Green marks what the system or the user does or has settled: primary actions, selection, reconciled or healthy state. It never stands for a channel or a severity.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Is Data Rule",
        "body": "Geist Mono is only for transaction IDs and payment references. Never use it for labels, numbers or decoration.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every amount, count, percentage and axis tick uses tabular numerals. Amounts follow the `12 500,00 MT` format.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Only Caps Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase belongs to the channel signs. Labels, headers and group names stay in sentence case.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Nested Cards Rule",
        "body": "A card never contains another card. Groupings inside a card are sunken tiles (`sunken`, 12px radius, no border, no shadow), dashed tiles for closed or empty states, or divided rows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** show every channel's money with its own sign and colour: the tag in rows, the solid segment in the highlighted chart month, the `-bar` tone at rest.",
      "**Do** keep all four channel tags identical in form: 4px radius, bold short caps, solid fill.",
      "**Do** use `danger` (#a3185e) for bad states and `warn` (#b45309) for needs-attention states, and keep e-Mola gold (#f2b705) for e-Mola alone.",
      "**Do** set every amount in tabular numerals with the `MT` unit, and put transaction IDs and references in Geist Mono.",
      "**Do** group content inside a card with sunken 12px tiles or divided rows.",
      "**Do** keep the \"Dados fictícios\" tag in the top bar while data is sample data.",
      "**Do** keep motion to 150–240ms ease-out state changes, and render final states under `prefers-reduced-motion`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use red for anything but M-Pesa. Not for errors, debt, or the notification dot.",
      "**Don't** use green for a channel, a severity, or decoration. It is for action, selection, and settled state.",
      "**Don't** put a card inside a card.",
      "**Don't** use mono for labels, headings, or amounts.",
      "**Don't** add uppercase labels or eyebrow text above headings. Uppercase belongs only to channel signs.",
      "**Don't** show one blended revenue total in a single colour where the amount could be split by channel.",
      "**Don't** use the pop shadow on cards at rest."
    ]
  }
}